1
00:00:15,670 --> 00:00:18,500
I never dreamed before

2
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:21,340
I'm gonna knock the door

3
00:00:21,340 --> 00:00:24,910
into the world of perfect free

4
00:00:24,910 --> 00:00:27,010
(You ain't no lonely!)

5
00:00:27,010 --> 00:00:29,850
You're gonna say I'm lying

6
00:00:29,850 --> 00:00:32,580
I'm gonna get the chance

7
00:00:32,580 --> 00:00:36,150
I thought a chance is far from me

8
00:00:36,150 --> 00:00:37,320
(You ain't no lonely!)

9
00:00:37,320 --> 00:00:40,230
I was made to hit in America

10
00:00:40,230 --> 00:00:43,090
(I was made to hit in America)

11
00:00:43,090 --> 00:00:49,000
I was made to hit in America

12
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,670
You are the sun, you are the star

13
00:00:52,670 --> 00:00:54,670
(To me, forever)

14
00:00:54,670 --> 00:00:58,380
You are the sun, you are the star

15
00:00:58,380 --> 00:01:01,610
(To me, forever)

16
00:01:08,450 --> 00:01:14,060
I was made to hit in America

17
00:01:14,060 --> 00:01:16,900
I was made to hit in America

18
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:19,760
(I was made to hit in America)

19
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:22,570
I was made to hit in America

20
00:01:22,570 --> 00:01:25,340
(I was made to hit in America)

21
00:01:25,340 --> 00:01:33,210
I was made to hit in America

22
00:01:52,930 --> 00:01:54,230
Huh?

23
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:57,330
Did you get the shell?

24
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:00,630
You?

25
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:05,010
Just answer my question.

26
00:02:05,010 --> 00:02:06,610
It'll be all good.

27
00:02:06,610 --> 00:02:11,120
All the white dudes will be sad
if Eddy Lee's dead, right?

28
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:14,290
For me, I don't give a fuck!

29
00:02:14,290 --> 00:02:15,950
Who told you to do this?

30
00:02:15,950 --> 00:02:18,460
Hey! Hey!

31
00:02:18,460 --> 00:02:19,790
I'm asking you!

32
00:02:19,790 --> 00:02:23,280
Where the fuck is this thing you stole?

33
00:02:26,630 --> 00:02:27,800
Say what?

34
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:30,970
Whoa Eddy! Are you all right?

35
00:02:30,970 --> 00:02:35,310
Yeah. He took off right when
the security guys came in.

36
00:02:35,310 --> 00:02:37,910
I see. You are still lucky.

37
00:02:37,910 --> 00:02:40,250
I knew it! He found out everything.

38
00:02:40,250 --> 00:02:43,420
Can't be. How could he find out?

39
00:02:43,420 --> 00:02:45,250
Ray, the movie's done.

40
00:02:45,250 --> 00:02:48,250
Our tour movie, that Jim directed.

41
00:02:48,250 --> 00:02:49,250
Yeah?

42
00:02:49,250 --> 00:02:52,920
Yeah, they've been previewing it
a couple of times last week...

43
00:02:52,920 --> 00:02:53,930
What?

44
00:02:53,930 --> 00:02:57,760
Yeah, I told Jim to cut out
the scene of me playing, "Lucille."

45
00:02:57,760 --> 00:03:00,730
You know, he's an artist.

46
00:03:00,730 --> 00:03:01,720
Well...

47
00:03:03,270 --> 00:03:06,940
Yeah, it was the uh...
It was the scene of Koyuki.

48
00:03:06,940 --> 00:03:09,600
You know, singing really, really good.

49
00:03:20,550 --> 00:03:25,490
"Live 16 'Indies'"

50
00:03:43,570 --> 00:03:45,440
I'll come again!

51
00:03:46,580 --> 00:03:48,180
What's with that kid?

52
00:03:48,180 --> 00:03:51,080
He comes in everyday, smiling.
Gives me the creeps.

53
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:57,090
I hear if you keep staring at a Telecaster,
it helps you endure even hard labor.

54
00:03:57,090 --> 00:03:58,920
Oh...

55
00:03:58,920 --> 00:04:00,150
But...

56
00:04:01,430 --> 00:04:03,790
He'd better make up his mind
or it'll be sold.

57
00:04:09,770 --> 00:04:12,770
Hey! Hey!

58
00:04:12,770 --> 00:04:14,610
Where're the spring rolls?!

59
00:04:14,610 --> 00:04:16,130
Oh sorry!

60
00:04:17,610 --> 00:04:20,450
Hey Tanaka! The dumplings are overdone.

61
00:04:20,450 --> 00:04:22,610
I just got a complaint.

62
00:04:22,610 --> 00:04:25,080
-I'm sorry!
-Hey, spring rolls!

63
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:25,980
Right!

64
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:31,690
Hey Tanaka!

65
00:04:31,690 --> 00:04:35,790
You didn't ladle the soup carefully!
The same customer is complaining!

66
00:04:35,790 --> 00:04:37,120
I'm sorry.

67
00:04:43,570 --> 00:04:46,400
Strange...I'm doing it properly.

68
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:47,570
My goodness!

69
00:04:47,570 --> 00:04:53,080
-How many times must I complain
before you get things right?!
-I'm so sorry.

70
00:04:53,080 --> 00:04:59,420
-How can I pay for this?
-Huh? It's Saito-san...

71
00:04:59,420 --> 00:05:03,220
I thought they'd give me a free meal.

72
00:05:05,090 --> 00:05:09,260
-What a stingy shop.
-You're the stingy one!

73
00:05:09,260 --> 00:05:11,930
I'm counting on you for Tuesday.

74
00:05:11,930 --> 00:05:14,270
I have lots of deliveries.

75
00:05:14,270 --> 00:05:16,430
I guess I'll go to the bathhouse.

76
00:05:23,270 --> 00:05:25,900
Ouch!

77
00:05:35,620 --> 00:05:39,390
Maybe I'll go meet that girl who works
at the doughnut shop next door.

78
00:05:40,890 --> 00:05:44,230
Hey! Quit loafing and get back to work!

79
00:05:44,230 --> 00:05:45,960
Oh, sorry!

80
00:05:57,740 --> 00:06:00,080
He's so cool!

81
00:06:00,080 --> 00:06:03,250
Well, too bad! Yoshito belongs to me!

82
00:06:03,250 --> 00:06:05,750
No way! Yoshito's mine!

83
00:06:05,750 --> 00:06:08,480
-Hey!
-Excuse me!

84
00:06:09,390 --> 00:06:09,920
"Yoshito Morozumi"

85
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:11,820
"Yoshito Morozumi"

86
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:11,820
Is this guy popular?

87
00:06:11,820 --> 00:06:12,090
Is this guy popular?

88
00:06:12,090 --> 00:06:15,930
Are you serious? You don't
watch TV on Mondays at 8?

89
00:06:15,930 --> 00:06:18,360
It's a sad drama about
a short-distance runner.

90
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:20,260
I sooo love it!

91
00:06:20,260 --> 00:06:25,100
Yoshito plays a young guy in
a wheelchair. And he's awesome.

92
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:28,500
Oh...

93
00:06:34,110 --> 00:06:36,880
Good, we had a good crowd tonight.

94
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:38,880
I'm totally beat!

95
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:42,080
-You'll get paid nicely tonight.
-Really?

96
00:06:44,890 --> 00:06:46,960
Hey Tanaka-kun!

97
00:06:46,960 --> 00:06:50,230
There's a female customer
named Minami asking for you.

98
00:06:50,230 --> 00:06:53,030
Huh? Maho?

99
00:06:53,030 --> 00:06:55,030
She's quite cute.

100
00:06:55,030 --> 00:06:56,270
Your girlfriend?

101
00:06:56,270 --> 00:06:57,930
No...nothing like that.

102
00:07:06,910 --> 00:07:08,380
Hi!

103
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:17,920
Hey, doesn't that boy look familiar?

104
00:07:17,920 --> 00:07:19,980
Huh?

105
00:07:22,430 --> 00:07:26,020
-He's the one in the drama.
-A-And that water commercial!

106
00:07:27,270 --> 00:07:31,100
-Ryusuke told me you worked here.
-Oh...

107
00:07:31,100 --> 00:07:33,270
You sure are working hard.

108
00:07:33,270 --> 00:07:36,370
Nah...Not really.

109
00:07:36,370 --> 00:07:40,140
Oh yeah, let me introduce you...
This is one of my classmates, Yoshito.

110
00:07:41,210 --> 00:07:46,050
We met once in Mi-chan's shop.
You're on TV, right? That's awesome.

111
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:50,560
Hey Maho...this guy looks so dirty.

112
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:52,350
You sure the food here is okay?

113
00:07:54,560 --> 00:07:57,730
-Koyuki, are you free on Monday?
-Why?

114
00:07:57,730 --> 00:08:00,060
It's Christine's birthday party.

115
00:08:00,060 --> 00:08:02,900
I wondered if you could come.

116
00:08:02,900 --> 00:08:05,400
Christine?

117
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:06,400
What?

118
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:10,340
I thought we were gonna have this party
only with friends from school.

119
00:08:10,340 --> 00:08:13,240
Why not? It's always more fun
with more people.

120
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:16,080
What do you mean?
We already have enough people.

121
00:08:16,080 --> 00:08:18,070
Why are you so unhappy about it?

122
00:08:19,620 --> 00:08:24,450
-Wow! They're bilingual!
-And she's so pretty.

123
00:08:28,260 --> 00:08:30,760
They were eating the 5000-yen course.

124
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:34,390
Hope they have money.

125
00:08:43,870 --> 00:08:47,330
And I can't even speak English.

126
00:08:49,050 --> 00:08:51,050
Hey kid!

127
00:08:51,050 --> 00:08:53,640
Quit daydreaming!

128
00:08:55,390 --> 00:08:57,180
I'm sorry!

129
00:08:59,890 --> 00:09:03,520
No, thank you so much! Good-bye!

130
00:09:05,900 --> 00:09:08,070
Every label turned us down?

131
00:09:08,070 --> 00:09:11,300
Our self-produced CD is a total disaster.

132
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:15,170
We worked so hard on it.

133
00:09:17,070 --> 00:09:19,910
Ran's influence was worse than I expected.

134
00:09:19,910 --> 00:09:26,080
No one would come right out and say it,
but I could feel Ran's influence.

135
00:09:26,080 --> 00:09:29,750
Can we break through it? With our power?

136
00:09:29,750 --> 00:09:31,280
Ran...

137
00:09:35,930 --> 00:09:38,030
Lift up your heavy ass, now

138
00:09:38,030 --> 00:09:40,200
If you take off that stiff head

139
00:09:40,200 --> 00:09:41,800
You'll feel totally loose

140
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:42,870
This crazy, crazy world

141
00:09:42,870 --> 00:09:46,700
-Well...the sound is still amateur...

142
00:09:42,870 --> 00:09:46,700
-You just have to Stage Dive or Die

143
00:09:46,700 --> 00:09:49,040
-but I do feel some good vibes from it

144
00:09:46,700 --> 00:09:49,040
-Mind blower, a shower of sweat

145
00:09:49,040 --> 00:09:51,600
even with a name like Beck.

146
00:09:56,380 --> 00:09:58,050
However...

147
00:09:58,050 --> 00:10:01,220
these guys will never make a major debut.

148
00:10:01,220 --> 00:10:02,550
It's unfortunate,

149
00:10:02,550 --> 00:10:06,720
but anyone who crosses me
will be destroyed!

150
00:10:06,720 --> 00:10:08,560
Ran-san...

151
00:10:08,560 --> 00:10:14,430
Eiji, in this world,
only the strongest survive.

152
00:10:27,410 --> 00:10:30,040
In this world, power is everything.

153
00:10:32,920 --> 00:10:34,940
And Ran-san has it.

154
00:10:38,190 --> 00:10:41,860
And someone powerless like me,
just has to be smart and get around it.

155
00:10:41,860 --> 00:10:43,630
That's the reality.

156
00:10:43,630 --> 00:10:49,830
But Ryusuke, I'll become successful
no matter what I have to do.

157
00:10:58,580 --> 00:11:01,380
Ah...On the sixteenth?

158
00:11:01,380 --> 00:11:04,220
I can't. I got a red flag.

159
00:11:04,220 --> 00:11:08,390
Come on, Maho. My father's friend
opened an Italian restaurant.

160
00:11:08,390 --> 00:11:11,750
You know, in nighttime,
the view from there is so great.

161
00:11:19,060 --> 00:11:21,070
All right, I'll think about it.

162
00:11:21,070 --> 00:11:22,830
Oh, I gotta go to bathroom.

163
00:11:24,570 --> 00:11:26,900
What kind of band is Beck?

164
00:11:26,900 --> 00:11:30,200
They put their live [performance]
Before anything else.

165
00:11:31,240 --> 00:11:33,740
Well, I just met the singer.

166
00:11:33,740 --> 00:11:34,870
And?

167
00:11:38,580 --> 00:11:40,850
He was just a tiny tot.

168
00:11:46,760 --> 00:11:48,930
Yes, hello?

169
00:11:48,930 --> 00:11:51,100
Oh, I dialed the wrong number.

170
00:11:51,100 --> 00:11:53,600
Oh, it's Koyuki-kun?

171
00:11:53,600 --> 00:11:56,430
Uh...Yes.

172
00:11:56,430 --> 00:11:59,440
Maho is taking a shower
and can't come to the phone.

173
00:11:59,440 --> 00:12:01,940
Anything you want me to tell her?

174
00:12:01,940 --> 00:12:03,610
Oh?

175
00:12:03,610 --> 00:12:07,110
About Monday's party.

176
00:12:07,110 --> 00:12:09,110
Oh, the party...

177
00:12:09,110 --> 00:12:13,780
Come to the party dressed
like you were invited to a ball.

178
00:12:13,780 --> 00:12:16,450
And don't forget the present for the guest.

179
00:12:16,450 --> 00:12:18,050
And who...

180
00:12:27,130 --> 00:12:29,220
Hey, what're you laughing about?

181
00:12:34,640 --> 00:12:37,000
You're kind, Koyuki.

182
00:12:38,740 --> 00:12:42,080
But you don't seem to like my friends.

183
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:44,580
It's Christine's birthday party.

184
00:12:44,580 --> 00:12:47,280
I wondered if you could come.

185
00:13:23,120 --> 00:13:27,290
Hey you! This place is reserved today.

186
00:13:27,290 --> 00:13:29,960
Don't mess around here...please.

187
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:35,130
Err...no...My friend is enjoy party.

188
00:13:35,130 --> 00:13:37,570
Ah! Yoshito-kun!

189
00:13:37,570 --> 00:13:42,910
Sorry, but plans were changed.
Now this party is only for school friends.

190
00:13:42,910 --> 00:13:44,910
That's...

191
00:13:44,910 --> 00:13:48,080
So others can't come in. Sorry.

192
00:13:48,080 --> 00:13:50,580
Oh...

193
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:53,080
Please give this to Christine then.

194
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:54,080
Sure.

195
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:55,240
See ya!

196
00:14:10,270 --> 00:14:11,390
Why?!

197
00:14:13,100 --> 00:14:15,940
'Cause he really took it serious.

198
00:14:15,940 --> 00:14:17,930
He looked so stupid.

199
00:14:20,780 --> 00:14:22,340
Koyuki...

200
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:26,580
Hey! He don't give a fuck!

201
00:15:51,570 --> 00:15:53,060
The Telecaster is gone.

202
00:15:58,240 --> 00:16:00,510
Takano-san said to wait in the back.

203
00:16:03,580 --> 00:16:05,250
Hey!

204
00:16:05,250 --> 00:16:07,050
Hey! Wait!

205
00:16:08,250 --> 00:16:10,590
Takano-san wants...

206
00:16:10,590 --> 00:16:12,210
Hey!

207
00:16:14,430 --> 00:16:17,090
T-Thief!

208
00:16:17,090 --> 00:16:18,080
Huh?

209
00:16:20,100 --> 00:16:22,930
Takano...

210
00:16:22,930 --> 00:16:24,700
Crush!

211
00:16:44,220 --> 00:16:49,230
Katahira-san, how is that Telecaster?
I made lots of adjustments.

212
00:16:49,230 --> 00:16:51,060
Katahira...

213
00:16:51,060 --> 00:16:55,400
Ohh...It's nice. I wanna buy it.

214
00:16:55,400 --> 00:16:58,740
Huh? It's Tatsuya Katahira
of Loud Crime City.

215
00:16:58,740 --> 00:17:01,410
Can't do that. This kid's gonna buy it.

216
00:17:01,410 --> 00:17:03,410
I'll pay you double.

217
00:17:03,410 --> 00:17:09,180
-I didn't reserve it...
-No, Taira asked me.

218
00:17:10,480 --> 00:17:11,920
Oh...

219
00:17:11,920 --> 00:17:16,350
I'm a drummer, but I've gotta be nice
and give guitars a chance, too.

220
00:17:18,260 --> 00:17:21,590
If that kid doesn't buy it, let me know.

221
00:17:26,100 --> 00:17:29,330
Is Loud really going to disband
after their next live performance?

222
00:17:31,100 --> 00:17:34,270
Yup. You gotta know when to call it quits.

223
00:17:34,270 --> 00:17:37,540
Come watch us.

224
00:17:37,540 --> 00:17:41,880
Kid, the deadline is
the end of the month. Got it?

225
00:17:41,880 --> 00:17:43,010
Yes!

226
00:17:44,210 --> 00:17:47,220
Hmm...Katahira of Loud?

227
00:17:47,220 --> 00:17:48,220
Yup...

228
00:17:48,220 --> 00:17:51,720
It's true that Loud
is Japan's top rock band.

229
00:17:51,720 --> 00:17:54,060
Let's go see them at the Budokan.

230
00:17:54,060 --> 00:17:57,060
Stupid! It was sold out ages ago.

231
00:17:57,060 --> 00:18:00,560
Hah! So different from us.

232
00:18:00,560 --> 00:18:04,070
Loud wasn't popular from the start.

233
00:18:04,070 --> 00:18:05,930
Let's just concentrate on today's show.

234
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:10,240
Right! Live performances are important.

235
00:18:12,240 --> 00:18:15,750
But our problem right now is...

236
00:18:15,750 --> 00:18:17,240
This!

237
00:18:18,420 --> 00:18:22,420
We ordered 300 copies
and we have 210 left.

238
00:18:22,420 --> 00:18:24,420
That's 42 copies each!

239
00:18:24,420 --> 00:18:28,260
Friends, family, anyone you
can think of! Sell them all!

240
00:18:28,260 --> 00:18:31,760
B-But I don't know 40 people!

241
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:35,600
If we don't get rid of these,
we'll end up with a huge debt!

242
00:18:35,600 --> 00:18:36,530
-Oh...
-Oh...
-Oh...

243
00:18:41,210 --> 00:18:44,800
Yo! We're Beck!

244
00:18:46,210 --> 00:18:50,010
It's packed tonight,
but there's not much noise.

245
00:18:50,010 --> 00:18:52,220
They're all waiting for the next band.

246
00:18:52,220 --> 00:18:56,050
We should pump them up.

247
00:18:56,050 --> 00:18:57,580
One, two...

248
00:19:07,900 --> 00:19:09,020
Uh!

249
00:19:10,070 --> 00:19:11,360
Yeah!

250
00:19:14,570 --> 00:19:18,080
You open up the door
with negative aura

251
00:19:18,080 --> 00:19:19,910
You say future is murky indeed...

252
00:19:19,910 --> 00:19:22,750
I'm sick of hearing gripe.

253
00:19:22,750 --> 00:19:24,920
Open up the door with negative aura

254
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:26,080
If you never change

255
00:19:26,080 --> 00:19:29,920
It's probably the last time
I'll use this in a live performance.

256
00:19:26,080 --> 00:19:29,920
I think there is no way
my life fizzle out

257
00:19:29,920 --> 00:19:32,320
Thank you for all this time...
White Falcon.

258
00:19:33,590 --> 00:19:36,090
You open up the door with negative aura

259
00:19:36,090 --> 00:19:37,030
(I'm fed up fed up fed up)

260
00:19:37,030 --> 00:19:41,370
When Loud disbands,
Japanese rock will die.

261
00:19:37,030 --> 00:19:41,370
You say future is murky...

262
00:19:41,370 --> 00:19:45,040
And that's not an understatement.

263
00:19:45,040 --> 00:19:49,210
It's fact that Loud has carried
the Japanese scene on its shoulders.

264
00:19:49,210 --> 00:19:51,540
Really?

265
00:19:51,540 --> 00:19:56,240
And there's been no band
that can compare to Loud.

266
00:19:59,550 --> 00:20:01,550
Our gas ran out.

267
00:20:01,550 --> 00:20:02,720
Huh?

268
